Implementing Policies in Vault
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand HashiCorp Vault policy concepts and structure
Create and write access policies using HashiCorp Configuration Language (HCL)
Apply policies to control access to secrets and paths in Vault
Test and validate policy effectiveness through practical scenarios
Manage policy lifecycle including updates and deletions
Implement role-based access control using Vault policies
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with text editors (nano, vim, or similar)
Understanding of basic security concepts like authentication and authorization
Knowledge of JSON and basic configuration file formats
Completion of previous Vault labs or equivalent experience with Vault basics
