Task 3: Creating Basic Policies in HCL
Subtask 3.1: Create a Read-Only Policy
Create your first policy for read-only access to specific paths:

# Create read-only policy file
cat > policies/readonly-policy.hcl << 'EOF'
# Read-only policy for application secrets
path "secret/data/app/*" {
  capabilities = ["read", "list"]
}

# Allow listing of secret engines
path "secret/metadata" {
  capabilities = ["list"]
}

# Allow reading own token information
path "auth/token/lookup-self" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# Allow token renewal
path "auth/token/renew-self" {
  capabilities = ["update"]
}
EOF
Subtask 3.2: Create a Developer Policy
Create a policy for developers with broader access:

# Create developer policy file
cat > policies/developer-policy.hcl << 'EOF'
# Developer policy with read/write access to development secrets
path "secret/data/dev/*" {
  capabilities = ["create", "read", "update", "delete", "list"]
}

# Read access to shared configuration
path "secret/data/shared/config" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# List capabilities for secret metadata
path "secret/metadata/dev/*" {
  capabilities = ["list"]
}

# Allow developers to manage their own tokens
path "auth/token/lookup-self" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

path "auth/token/renew-self" {
  capabilities = ["update"]
}

path "auth/token/revoke-self" {
  capabilities = ["update"]
}
EOF
Subtask 3.3: Create an Admin Policy
Create a comprehensive admin policy:

# Create admin policy file
cat > policies/admin-policy.hcl << 'EOF'
# Admin policy with broad access
path "secret/*" {
  capabilities = ["create", "read", "update", "delete", "list"]
}

# Manage auth methods
path "auth/*" {
  capabilities = ["create", "read", "update", "delete", "list", "sudo"]
}

# Manage policies
path "sys/policies/acl/*" {
  capabilities = ["create", "read", "update", "delete", "list"]
}

# System configuration
path "sys/config/*" {
  capabilities = ["read", "update"]
}

# Audit logs
path "sys/audit" {
  capabilities = ["read", "list"]
}

# Health and status
path "sys/health" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# Manage tokens
path "auth/token/*" {
  capabilities = ["create", "read", "update", "delete", "list", "sudo"]
}
EOF
Task 4: Applying Policies to Control Access
Subtask 4.1: Load Policies into Vault
Apply the created policies to Vault:

# Load the read-only policy
vault policy write readonly-policy policies/readonly-policy.hcl

# Load the developer policy
vault policy write developer-policy policies/developer-policy.hcl

# Load the admin policy
vault policy write admin-policy policies/admin-policy.hcl

# Verify policies are loaded
vault policy list
Subtask 4.2: Create Test Data
Create some test secrets to work with:

# Enable KV v2 secrets engine if not already enabled
vault secrets enable -path=secret kv-v2

# Create test secrets for different paths
vault kv put secret/app/database username="app_user" password="app_pass123"
vault kv put secret/app/api-key key="api_key_12345" environment="production"

vault kv put secret/dev/database username="dev_user" password="dev_pass456"
vault kv put secret/dev/api-key key="dev_api_key_67890" environment="development"

vault kv put secret/shared/config timeout="30s" max_connections="100"

# Verify secrets are created
